---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from "../config";
---

<Base
  title="Support | Our Expenses"
  description="How Our Expenses splits a cost, where your data lives, and how to reach a human."
>
  <div class="shell prose">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="eyebrow">Its a one person project, please give me a day or two for answering :)</p>

    <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Write to <a href={"mailto:" + SUPPORT_EMAIL}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>. For a bug,
      tell me what you tapped, what you expected, what happened instead, and
      which iOS version you run.
    </p>

    <h2>How is a share calculated?</h2>
    <p>
      The app adds every income together, works out each person's weight within
      that sum, and applies the weight to the amount you typed. Three people
      earning 3000, 2000 and 1000 split a 600 expense into 300, 200 and 100.
    </p>

    <h2>How many people can I add?</h2>
    <p>Ten. The add form gives way to a note once you reach the cap.</p>

    <h2>Why didn't an old receipt change when I edited an income?</h2>
    <p>
      A saved expense keeps the split it was created with. Editing an income
      changes what the next expense produces and leaves your history untouched.
    </p>

    <h2>Where is my data?</h2>
    <p>
      In your iPhone's storage, nowhere else. The
      <a href="/privacy">&nbsp;privacy policy</a> covers the detail.
    </p>

    <h2>How do I delete an expense?</h2>
    <p>
      Open History and tap a row's checkbox to select it. Tapping anywhere else
      on the row opens its receipt instead. The delete button arms on the first
      press and commits on the second, so no single tap destroys anything.
      "Select all" covers your whole history, not just the rows on screen.
    </p>

    <h2>How do I remove someone?</h2>
    <p>
      On the People screen (top right button), press remove on their row. The row turns into a
      confirmation with a red tick to go through with it and a cross to back out.
      Removing a person leaves saved receipts alone, since each one carries its
      own split.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
